==Hindi==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sa|hi}} {{term|एक|sc=Deva|lang=sa|tr=éka}} (or a closely related Old-Indo-Aryan language, through Prakrit), from {{etyl|iir-pro|hi}} {{recons|Haykas|lang=iir-pro}} (compare Persian {{term|یک|tr=yek|lang=fa}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|hi}} {{recons|óynos|óykos||one, single|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Numeral===
'''एक''' (ek)

# {{cardinal|lang=hi}} [[one]] (1)
#: Number in Devanāgarī script: (१)
#: Number in Arabic script: (١)
#: Roman numeral: (I)

====Urdu spelling====
* {{ur-Arab|[[ایک]]}}

===Adjective===
{{hi-adj|tr=ek|ur=ایک}}

# [[one]]
# [[a]]
# [[sole]]
# [[only]]

